abstract: >-
  dwg2geo converts AutoCAD DWG engineering drawings to GeoJSON with two
  design commitments. It fails closed: georeferenced output is produced only
  when the source coordinate reference system is stated explicitly, and
  local-coordinate output only on explicit opt-in. And it is auditable:
  output is byte-deterministic for a given input and option set, and every
  conversion emits a machine-readable provenance record. One Rust core is
  exposed as a command-line tool, a WebAssembly module, a Python extension
  and an R package.
